Only un-assign beds when an ended visit actually has an active bed assignment, so ending a
visit of a patient who has no bed needs no bed write privilege.

openmrs-module-bedmanagement (7.2.0 and master) runs VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler
on every save of a visit that has a stop time, and it calls
BedManagementService.unAssignBedsInEndedVisit() unconditionally
(VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java:47-49). That method is annotated
@Authorized({"Assign Beds", "Edit Admission Locations"}, requireAll = true)
(BedManagementService.java:121), and the authorization advice checks it before the method
looks for an assignment. So every user who may end visits but not manage beds gets
"403 Assign Beds" when ending ANY visit, bed or no bed. In LiberiaEMR that is every login role
but the administrator: the queue roles end visits, and none of them should manage beds.

The fix asks getBedPatientAssignmentByVisit(uuid, false) first and calls
unAssignBedsInEndedVisit() only when it returns an assignment. That read needs "Get Beds" and
"Get Admission Locations", which every visit save already needs: the module's
VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentValidator calls the same method on every visit save. Ending a
visit that DOES hold a bed still requires both write privileges, unchanged.

Applied by distribution/backend/Dockerfile (bedmanagement stage), against
source.bedmanagement.commit in distribution/distro.properties (the 7.2.0 tag). Tracked in
packages/modify-pr/.patches/0005-openmrs-module-bedmanagement-end-visit-without-bed-write.md.

diff --git a/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java b/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
index 61f182f..2c6a063 100644
--- a/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
+++ b/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
@@ -44,8 +44,12 @@ public class VisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler implements SaveHandler<Vis
 	public void handle(Visit visit, User user, Date date, String s) {
 		if (visit.getVisitId() != null) {
 			
-			if (visit.getStopDatetime() != null) {
-				log.debug("Unassigning bed from patient (if any) due to stopped visit on " + visit.getStopDatetime());
+			// unAssignBedsInEndedVisit requires "Assign Beds" and "Edit Admission Locations", and this
+			// handler runs on every save of an ended visit. Only call it when there is a bed to free,
+			// so ending a visit of a patient who has no bed needs no bed write privilege.
+			if (visit.getStopDatetime() != null
+			        && !bedManagementService.getBedPatientAssignmentByVisit(visit.getUuid(), false).isEmpty()) {
+				log.debug("Unassigning bed from patient due to stopped visit on " + visit.getStopDatetime());
 				bedManagementService.unAssignBedsInEndedVisit(visit);
 			}
 		}
